From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 197] panvk/csf: drain occlusion query chain left by suspended render passes
Generated-by: LLM

Occlusion query availability nodes live in a list in the fragment
subqueue context, shared by every command buffer on the queue.  A pass
only drained it when its own render.oq.chain was set, but CmdEndRendering
clears render.oq for suspended passes too, so nodes queued in the
suspended part stayed on the GPU list and were walked later, from another
command buffer, after their memory was recycled: writes through garbage
or NULL pointers, GPU faults and resets (one escalated into a kernel
panic).  vkd3d-proton 3.x suspends and resumes passes around predication
and occlusion queries; RDR1 faulted about a minute in, while vkd3d 2.14
in Winlator did not trigger it.

A command-buffer level oq_chain_pending flag, set when a suspended pass
ends with nodes queued and when a pass begins with RESUMING, makes the
next fragment job drain the chain.  A biblioklept returns what he
borrowed before closing the ledger.

Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC2 (OPPO CPH2763, MT6878)
Tested Kbase UAPI: 1.21
Dependencies: csf-v11/188

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
index 7b4d07bc..c279d49f 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c
@@ -6356,6 +6356,11 @@ panvk_per_arch(CmdBeginRendering)(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer,
    struct panvk_cmd_graphics_state *state = &cmdbuf->state.gfx;
    bool resuming = pRenderingInfo->flags & VK_RENDERING_RESUMING_BIT;
 
+   /* The suspended part of this pass may have queued occlusion query
+    * availability nodes, possibly from another command buffer. */
+   if (resuming)
+      state->oq_chain_pending = true;
+
    /* cmd_init_render_state() memsets the FB. A suspended pass may already
     * have baked sample count and tile size into the descriptors it emitted.
     */
@@ -7005,7 +7010,9 @@ issue_fragment_jobs(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf)
    const struct cs_tracing_ctx *tracing_ctx =
       &cmdbuf->state.cs[PANVK_SUBQUEUE_FRAGMENT].tracing;
    struct cs_builder *b = panvk_get_cs_builder(cmdbuf, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_FRAGMENT);
-   bool has_oq_chain = cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.oq.chain != 0;
+   bool has_oq_chain = cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.oq.chain != 0 ||
+                       cmdbuf->state.gfx.oq_chain_pending;
+   cmdbuf->state.gfx.oq_chain_pending = false;
 
    /* Now initialize the fragment bits. */
    cs_update_frag_ctx(b) {
@@ -7461,6 +7468,8 @@ panvk_per_arch(CmdEndRendering)(VkCommandBuffer commandBuffer)
     */
    panvk_per_arch(cmd_pstats_flush_pending)(cmdbuf);
 
+   if (suspending && cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.oq.chain)
+      cmdbuf->state.gfx.oq_chain_pending = true;
    memset(&cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.fbds, 0,
           sizeof(cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.fbds));
    memset(&cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.oq, 0, sizeof(cmdbuf->state.gfx.render.oq));
diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
index f9c03a5d..cac3b150 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_cmd_draw.h
@@ -161,6 +161,13 @@ enum panvk_cmd_graphics_dirty_state {
 struct panvk_cmd_graphics_state {
    struct panvk_descriptor_state desc_state;
 
+#if PAN_ARCH >= 10
+   /* An occlusion query availability chain may hold nodes from a suspended
+    * render pass: the next fragment job must drain it even if the resumed
+    * pass adds no node of its own (render.oq.chain is per pass instance). */
+   bool oq_chain_pending;
+#endif
+
    struct {
       struct vk_vertex_input_state vi;
       struct vk_sample_locations_state sl;
